/-!
# The chain of `g = I₀² K₀²` in the class `PDom`

Generated by `tools/gen_domg.py`.  With `pB4 = θ pB3`, `pB5 = θ pB4` (`LaplaceDecay.lean` has `pB0 … pB3`):

* `thGk_eq_P`: `θᵏ g = Σᵢ C(k,i) pBᵢ pB_{k-i}` (polynomial identities);
* at infinity (`t > 0`): `|t² θᵏ g| ≤ Mₖ`, and `|t⁴ (θ+2)ᵐ g|` bounded for `m = 1, 2, 3` (`|t pBᵢ|` and
  `|t³ (pBⱼ + pBⱼ₊₁)|` are bounded, `LaplaceDecay.lean`);
* near `0` (`0 < t ≤ 1`): `|pBᵢ| ≤ kᵢ e (1 + log(2/t))`, so `√t |f| ≤ C` for every function of the chains;
* the auxiliary chains `gQ1 = (θ+2)²g`, `gQ2 = (θ+2)³g`, `gR = 16t²(θ+2)g - P₃(θ)g = -θ⁵g/(4t²)` with their
  `θ` and `θ²`, as `HasDerivAt` chains;
* **`pdom_thG0` … `pdom_gR2`**: all fifteen functions are in `PDom`, and `t⁴ |f| ≤ C` on `[1, ∞)` for
  `f = gQ1, gQ2, gR` (`pdom4_gQ1`, `pdom4_gQ2`, `pdom4_gR`): the hypotheses of R1 and R2 of `AJ.lean`.
-/

